<section class="section">
  <h2>What it does</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">
    An agent that talks to OpenAI, Ollama, llama.cpp, vLLM or OpenRouter through
    the same API ends up writing the same plumbing: pooled clients, retries,
    streaming, and working out what each server refuses. This package is that
    plumbing, extracted from three servers that had each written it separately
    and drifted apart. Prompts, tools and what a run is for stay with the caller.
  </p>

  <ul class="card-grid">
    <li>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Tool schemas a server accepts</h3>
        <p>
          <code>sanitizeTools</code> makes an MCP tool schema something a strict
          or grammar-constrained server will take, and <code>negotiate</code>
          re-sends a request without what the endpoint or the model refused.
        </p>
      </article>
    </li>
    <li>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Tools loaded on demand</h3>
        <p>
          A name-only catalogue plus a <code>load_tools</code> meta-tool, so a
          run pays for the schemas the model asks for instead of all of them on
          every request.
        </p>
      </article>
    </li>
    <li>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>One turn, or the whole loop</h3>
        <p>
          <code>runTurn</code> is one streamed turn with retry and negotiation
          around it; <code>runAgentLoop</code> runs it per step, with the tool
          calls between, until the model stops asking.
        </p>
      </article>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="section" id="start">
  <h2>Get started</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      ESM only, Node 22 or later. <code>openai</code> (version 6 or later) is a
      peer dependency.
    </p>
    <pre class="code"><code>npm install @cubicecho/agent-core openai</code></pre>
    <pre class="code"><code>import { runAgentLoop } from "@cubicecho/agent-core";

const { turn } = await runAgentLoop({
  config: {
    baseUrl: "http://localhost:11434/v1", // any OpenAI-compatible endpoint
    apiKey: "",
    model: "qwen3",
    maxTokens: 1024,
    temperature: 0.2,
    maxToolIterations: 8,
  },
  messages: [{ role: "user", content: "What changed in the last release?" }],
  tools, // OpenAI tool definitions, if the run has any
  dispatch: async ({ name, args }) =&gt; callTool(name, args), // returns what the model reads
});

console.log(turn.content);</code></pre>
  </div>

  <p class="readme-link">
